### F. QUALITY 105: the lesson's drafted block vs the landed criterion
--- lesson block at 9cf0146b94ddba12d454ebf7288ce6e5c5d535bb ---
## QUALITY criterion (drafted; lands with the round commit)

- **105. A counter arm that reads a directory by pathspec is proven on a tree
  where the arm must fire (the positive control), not only on the do-nothing
  tree. Falsifier: a control receipt in which the arm's own counter reads zero
  (the arm never fired); a pathspec that returns the directory itself is a
  defect even when the overall verdict is false for another reason.**

## The method (for the round report)
--- landed criterion at 9cf0146b94ddba12d454ebf7288ce6e5c5d535bb (falsifier sentence) ---
1586:A counter arm that reads a directory, a revision or a manifest is proven by a positive control in which that arm must fire: the receipt records the arm's own non-zero count at a tree where the round's work is present. The do-nothing tree cannot prove an arm live — it fails for other reasons, so a dead arm (a pathspec that matches nothing, a key that never appears) looks healthy there. The check that can fail: a positive-control receipt in which the arm's own counter reads zero, or a control run that pre-registers the arm's value without a tree that carries it.

